  <prompt>
    Repoint the client-side launch points that open the retiring sprk_analysisworkspace surface so they call openSpaarkeAi
    (`sprk_spaarkeai`) instead, and remove the dead custom-page path that targets sprk_analysisworkspace_8bc0b. Covers the
    sprk_analysis form OnLoad/ribbon command, the AnalysisWorkspace launcher shim, and the PlaybookLibrary navigateTo.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Dataverse web-resource JS launch commands, code-page navigateTo, and the
    openSpaarkeAi client deep-link. Follow ADRs strictly — record-driven opens stay in code via openSpaarkeAi, not
    surfaceLaunchRegistry.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The sprk_analysis form OnLoad/ribbon launcher and the PlaybookLibrary navigateTo open the sprk_spaarkeai surface via
    openSpaarkeAi; the dead custom-page path (sprk_analysisworkspace_8bc0b) in sprk_analysis_commands.js is removed; a Grep
    for the retiring names across client JS/TS returns zero (outside files deleted by 063); client builds green.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Per spec §13.5 / FR-19, client launch points still open the retiring code page. Three exist:
      sprk_analysis_commands.js (Spaarke_OpenAnalysisWorkspace at lines ~145-169, ~213-235, and a dead custom-page branch
      near 549 targeting sprk_analysisworkspace_8bc0b); the AnalysisWorkspace launcher shim
      sprk_AnalysisWorkspaceLauncher.js; and PlaybookLibrary main.tsx (~234-245) which navigateTo webresourceName
      sprk_AnalysisWorkspace. Task 060 already repointed the server deep-links; this repoints the client. openSpaarkeAi is
      the target (extended in 052). The AnalysisWorkspace launcher tree itself is deleted in 063 — here we only repoint the
      launch callers that survive (form/ribbon + PlaybookLibrary) and strip the dead branch.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/webresources/js/sprk_analysis_commands.js</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/PlaybookLibrary/src/main.tsx</file>
